# ProductCatalog: the routes @cap-ts/soap-adapter mounts for a SOAP service (/soap/<@path>/<Entity>).
# The producer-catalog terminal logs every SOAP call with its input: compare it with each request below.

@server = http://localhost:4004/soap/catalog
@auth = Basic alice:alice


### -------------------------------------------------------------- Products (FindProducts)

### No query options: the runtime reads every product and answers a page of cds.query.soap.pageSize (4) with an
### @odata.nextLink. Every row carries Channel: the backend echoes the SOAP header the header() hook sent.
GET {{server}}/Products
Authorization: {{auth}}

### The next page: the link repeats the query, $skiptoken advances
GET {{server}}/Products?$skiptoken=4
Authorization: {{auth}}

### Everything expressible in the operation's input (Category, SortBy, MaxHits): the request() hook sets
### __filterPushedDown and the backend's answer is the page (see the SOAP log: Category, SortBy, Descending, MaxHits)
GET {{server}}/Products?$filter=Category eq 'Furniture'&$orderby=Price desc&$top=2&$select=ProductID,Name,Price
Authorization: {{auth}}

### Not all of it expressible (contains is case-sensitive, the backend's NameContains is not): the input narrows the
### answer, the runtime filters, sorts and pages in memory
GET {{server}}/Products?$filter=contains(Name,'Desk')&$orderby=Name&$select=ProductID,Name
Authorization: {{auth}}

### The response() hook turned the backend's 'X' into a Boolean; $count is the total before paging
GET {{server}}/Products?$filter=Discontinued eq true&$select=ProductID,Name,Discontinued&$count=true
Authorization: {{auth}}

### Nested values (@Soap.path: 'Supplier.Name') and a value with an XML attribute (<Price currency="EUR">: its $value)
GET {{server}}/Products?$select=ProductID,Price,Currency,SupplierName,SupplierCountry&$top=3
Authorization: {{auth}}

### Filter functions evaluated by the runtime (startswith, tolower, contains) and in(...) on a field
GET {{server}}/Products?$filter=startswith(tolower(Name),'office') or contains(Name,'Lamp') or Category in ('Furniture')&$select=ProductID,Name
Authorization: {{auth}}

### endswith, a null literal and a negative number, evaluated by the runtime
GET {{server}}/Products?$filter=endswith(Name,'Desk') or (SupplierName ne null and Price lt -1)&$select=ProductID,Name
Authorization: {{auth}}

### not before a parenthesised condition and before a function; and binds tighter than or
GET {{server}}/Products?$filter=not (Category eq 'Electronics') and not startswith(Name,'Office') or ProductID eq 'P001'&$select=ProductID,Name,Category
Authorization: {{auth}}

### concat and substring (zero-based), evaluated by the runtime: the products of suppliers in AT whose name starts "Sta"
GET {{server}}/Products?$filter=concat(concat(SupplierCountry,'-'),Category) eq 'AT-Furniture' and substring(Name,0,3) eq 'Sta'&$select=ProductID,Name
Authorization: {{auth}}

### A function on the left of a comparison (length, tolower)
GET {{server}}/Products?$filter=length(Name) gt 18 or tolower(Category) eq 'office supplies'&$select=ProductID,Name
Authorization: {{auth}}

### A doubled quote stays one quote of the value: no product is named It's
GET {{server}}/Products?$filter=Name eq 'It''s'&$count=true
Authorization: {{auth}}

### multipleSelection: true (@Soap.filterRestriction): ProductID in (...) stays one FindProducts call, the request()
### hook passes the list (see the SOAP log: "ProductID":["P001","P004"])
GET {{server}}/Products?$filter=ProductID in ('P001','P004')&$select=ProductID,Name
Authorization: {{auth}}

### $skip with $top: applied by the backend (MaxHits, Skip); $search is accepted and ignored (every product counts)
GET {{server}}/Products?$skip=6&$top=2&$select=ProductID
Authorization: {{auth}}

###
GET {{server}}/Products?$search=desk&$select=ProductID&$count=true
Authorization: {{auth}}

### The short routes: the same entity without the /soap prefix (/<path>/<Entity>, also by key)
GET http://localhost:4004/catalog/Products/P004
Authorization: {{auth}}

### A literal on the left of a comparison: 400 (the parser fails closed, nothing is ignored)
GET {{server}}/Products?$filter='Standing Desk' eq Name
Authorization: {{auth}}

### Read by key (the key value is compared with the first key element)
GET {{server}}/Products/P004
Authorization: {{auth}}

### No row: 404
GET {{server}}/Products/P999
Authorization: {{auth}}

### $expand is not a query option of the SOAP routes: 400
GET {{server}}/Products?$expand=Supplier
Authorization: {{auth}}

### A malformed $filter: 400 (the parser fails closed, nothing is ignored)
GET {{server}}/Products?$filter=Name eq
Authorization: {{auth}}


### -------------------------------------------------------------- Stock (GetStock: one product per call)

### One product: one SOAP call; Available is computed by an after('READ') handler of the adapter class
GET {{server}}/Stock?$filter=ProductID eq 'P004'
Authorization: {{auth}}

### multipleSelection: false: in(...) on the key is fanned out, one SOAP call per value (see the SOAP log), merged,
### then ordered and counted
GET {{server}}/Stock?$filter=ProductID in ('P001','P002','P003')&$orderby=Available desc&$count=true
Authorization: {{auth}}

### mandatoryFields: a filter without ProductID is 400 MISSING_MANDATORY_FILTER
GET {{server}}/Stock
Authorization: {{auth}}

### in(...) on the key beside an OR can not be fanned out: 400 UNSUPPORTED_MULTI_SELECTION_FILTER
GET {{server}}/Stock?$filter=ProductID in ('P001') or Warehouse eq 'Munich'
Authorization: {{auth}}


### -------------------------------------------------------------- The same service as CAP serves it

### cds.query.soap.agentHints: the $metadata carries "SOAP hints: Every read needs a filter on ProductID ..." on
### Stock and on its element ProductID (Core.Description); an MCP describe of a projection on it shows the same
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/$metadata
Authorization: {{auth}}

### The SOAP service is also an OData V4 service of the application: reads run the same pipeline
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/Products?$filter=Category eq 'Furniture'&$select=ProductID,Name
Authorization: {{auth}}

### The filter restriction holds on every way in, not only on the /soap routes: no ProductID, 400
### MISSING_MANDATORY_FILTER before any SOAP call
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/Stock
Authorization: {{auth}}

### ... and a key list is one GetStock call per value (see the SOAP log), merged and sorted
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/Stock?$filter=ProductID in ('P002','P005')&$orderby=ProductID desc
Authorization: {{auth}}

### Read by key: the key is the mandatory filter
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/Stock('P004')
Authorization: {{auth}}

### Read only: writes are 405
POST http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/Products
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ProductID": "P099", "Name": "New" }
